 "result_text": "I changed the data format 3 check in `ruuvitag_sensor/ruuvi.py` so it accepts the shorter payloads that RuuviFW 1.2.8 sends. I haven't run the tests or tried it against real sensor data.\n\nBefore, `_get_data_format_3` rejected anything that wasn't exactly 54 hex characters, which is why the trimmed trailing NULLs broke it. It now accepts any payload of at least 44 characters. That is the 16-character prefix plus the 14 bytes (28 characters) the decoder reads. The `03` format byte check is unchanged. The decoder only reads the first 14 bytes, so extra trailing bytes on older firmware still decode fine.\n\nI did not implement #29, since the task was only to resolve this bug.",
